{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483045-if-covenants-orders-courts-etc-had-werewolf-style-tribal-vows-what-would-they-be","id":1483045,"title":"If covenants/orders/courts/etc. had Werewolf-style tribal vows, what would they be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-04T09:58:15-07:00","id":1483045,"title":"If covenants/orders/courts/etc. had Werewolf-style tribal vows, what would they be?","content":"Title says it all (I hope). If the social splats of other gamelines had their own tribal vows a la WtF, what would they be? I think I have a few ideas about the Invictus and Adamantine Arrow, but I'd like to see other people's takes first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26974-dreamwave","name":"Dreamwave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T13:39:40-07:00","id":1483506,"title":"","content":"Speaking to Mage, the Orders do sort of have their own equivalent of the vows; the &quot;Magic is...&quot; format.<br /> <br /> That said, there's potential for an interesting vow around how the Orders treat language. Like, the Arrow believe in keeping your word in spirit, the Mysterium don't tell lies, whilst the Ladder seem to be highly legalistic in their emphasis on precise wording.<br /> The Guardians and Freaks are a little less clear to me. Maybe the Guardians <i>Always </i>lie? I dunno.<br /> <br /> I think the focus on language is reasonable due to High Speech being such a core element of the splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T01:18:28-07:00","id":1484094,"title":"","content":"It would be really cool to see something resembling a Tribe's favoured prey for the Vampire covenants:<br /> <br /> Carthians: Feed from those in power<br /> Circle of the Crone: Feed from those who resist their passions<br /> Lancea et Sanctum: Feed from mortal sinners<br /> The Invictus: Feed from those who submit to you<br /> The Ordo Dracul: Feed on exceptional mortals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T13:29:56-07:00","id":1484132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483045-if-covenants-orders-courts-etc-had-werewolf-style-tribal-vows-what-would-they-be?p=1484094#post1484094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be really cool to see something resembling a Tribe's favoured prey for the Vampire covenants:<br /> <br /> Carthians: Feed from those in power<br /> Circle of the Crone: Feed from those who resist their passions<br /> Lancea et Sanctum: Feed from mortal sinners<br /> The Invictus: Feed from those who submit to you<br /> The Ordo Dracul: Feed on exceptional mortals</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes me think of a kind of shortened 'Path of Enlightenment' from Masquerade. Like, each Covenant feeding on a certain group they feel they can justify to themselves. Fits particularly nicely with the paradoxes at the hearts of the Carthians and LeS. <br /> <br /> The Ordo might not fit with that... I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}